(7723112, 1271409, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> Interesting viewpoint and photograph. I''m guessing there''s some partial desat going on and I''m not sure how I feel about that. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>There wasn''t any selective desaturation here Lynn, just a straight color photo. Different sections of the stairs are illuminated by lights with different color temperature, that''s all.</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyStreet: Interesting viewpoint and photograph. I''m guessing there''s some partial desat going on and I''m not sure how I feel about that.  There wasn''t any selective desaturation here Lynn, just a straight color photo. Different sections of the stairs are illuminated by lights with different color temperature, that''s all.', '2022-07-08 11:38:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7723115, 1271409, 100831, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> Interesting viewpoint and photograph. I''m guessing there''s some partial desat going on and I''m not sure how I feel about that. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>There wasn''t any selective desaturation here Lynn, just a straight color photo. Different sections of the stairs are illuminated by lights with different color temperature, that''s all. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Interesting lighting too then! I''m sure it would also look well in b/w but I''m glad to have seen the colors.</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Originally posted by PennyStreet: Interesting viewpoint and photograph. I''m guessing there''s some partial desat going on and I''m not sure how I feel about that.  There wasn''t any selective desaturation here Lynn, just a straight color photo. Different sections of the stairs are illuminated by lights with different color temperature, that''s all.   Interesting lighting too then! I''m sure it would also look well in b/w but I''m glad to have seen the colors.', '2022-07-08 13:04:00.000000', NULL, 0),
